  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of the inadequate and poorly usable kitchen/dining facilities for six occupiers, including its long and narrow layout, the need to take bicycles through this space to access the rear garden cycle storage, and the poor relationship between the second-floor bedroom and ground-floor kitchen, would fail to provide a satisfactory standard of accommodation for future occupiers. The layout would not provide a practical, safe or convenient communal living space and would result in substandard living conditions, contrary to Sections 2 and 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policies D5 and D6 of the London Plan 2021, Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010, and Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the cooking appliances found within individual bedrooms and their use and poor usability of the shared kitchen/dining room, would fail to provide a genuine shared HMO arrangement. The accommodation would operate more like a bedsit-style layout, with occupiers likely to cook and eat within their own rooms rather than using shared facilities. This would undermine the communal nature expected of a HMO and would result in a poor standard of accommodation, contrary to Sections 2 and 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policies D5 and D6 of the London Plan 2021, Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010, and Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014."
  ],
